From: Christoph Kaser <christoph@caser.de>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:35:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rs-matter: allow Thread attachment before a BLE command response

BTP acknowledgements confirm transport delivery, not command completion.
ConnectNetwork can take more than five seconds while the accessory searches
for a Thread parent. Keep the transport acknowledgement timer unchanged and
allow sixty seconds for the Matter response. The commissioner still enforces
its overall session deadline.

--- a/rs-matter/src/transport/session.rs
+++ b/rs-matter/src/transport/session.rs
@@ -66,9 +66,11 @@
 
 /// Receive timeout for a BTP (BLE) session.
 ///
-/// BTP runs its own acknowledgement scheme underneath, so the MRP ladder does not
-/// describe it; this matches the BTP layer's own ack timeout.
-const BTP_RX_TIMEOUT_MS: u64 = 5_000;
+/// A BTP acknowledgement confirms delivery, not completion of a Matter command.
+/// In particular, ConnectNetwork may be waiting for Thread attachment long after
+/// the request has been acknowledged. Allow that processing time independently
+/// of BTP's transport acknowledgement timer.
+const BTP_RX_TIMEOUT_MS: u64 = 60_000;
 
 pub const MAX_CAT_IDS_PER_NOC: usize = 3;
 pub type NocCatIds = [u32; MAX_CAT_IDS_PER_NOC];
@@ -2260,7 +2262,7 @@
         );
         assert_eq!(
             session(Address::Btp(BtAddr([0; 6]))).rx_timeout_ms(300),
-            BTP_RX_TIMEOUT_MS
+            60_000 // Allow slow Thread ConnectNetwork responses over BLE.
         );
 
         // UDP sums both directions of the MRP ladder plus the processing
